description:
Design a n-bit wide ring counter implemented using m flip-flops. On each clock cycle, the counter shifts the value of the last flip-flop into the first position, creating a circular rotation of the bit pattern. This results in a series of outputs representing a single '1' that moves through the bits in a circular fashion, thus generating a sequence useful for various timing and control applications. The module's parameters allow customization of the number of outputs and flip-flops, with the output reflecting the state of the ring counter.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg [n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg [n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of output signals
parameter m = 4; // number of flip-flops in the ring

reg [m-1:0] flip_flops;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  flip_flops <= {flip_flops[m-2:0], flip_flops[m-1]};
end

assign out = flip_flops[n-1:0];

endmodule

