Design a 32-bit multiplier circuit. The module takes a 32-bit input and performs a series of arithmetic shifts and additions to calculate the product. The final output is generated by manipulating the input value with different bit shifts and combinatorial logic, ultimately yielding the scaled result based on the input data.
