description:
Design a one-bit full adder circuit. The module takes three one-bit inputs: two significant bits (a and b) and a carry-in (cin). It produces a one-bit sum output and a carry-out (cout). The sum output is the result of the XOR operation applied to the inputs, while the carry-out is generated using AND and OR logic to account for the carry conditions between the inputs.
module top_module(
    input a, b, cin,
    output cout, sum
);

code:
module top_module(
    input a, b, cin,
    output cout, sum
);wire w1, w2, w3;

    // XOR gate for sum calculation
    xor(sum, a, b, cin);

    // AND gate for carry-out calculation
    and(w1, a, b);
    and(w2, a, cin);
    and(w3, b, cin);
    or(cout, w1, w2, w3);

endmodule

